<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Sections>

  Longer documents are divided into sections. In order to start a new
  section, select <menu|Insert|Section|Section>, or type
  <key|\\ s e c t i o n> followed by <key|return>. The cursor is now inside
  an empty section title, and the status bar indicates
  <verbatim|section>:

  <\big-envbox>
    <section*|1<space|1em><small-focus|<text-cursor>>>
  </big-envbox>

  Type the title of the section, say \PMy new section\Q, and press
  <key|return>. The cursor leaves the title and goes to a new paragraph,
  where you type the body of your section:

  <\big-envbox>
    <section*|1<space|1em>My new section>

    The body of my section.<text-cursor>
  </big-envbox>

  Sections are numbered automatically, in the <tmstyle|generic> style as in
  the <tmstyle|article> style. If
  you insert a new section before the existing ones, the following sections
  are renumbered, and so are the references to them. The way in which
  sections are numbered and displayed only depends on the style: when you
  switch from <tmstyle|article> to <tmstyle|book>, the sections keep their
  titles but take the layout of the book style.

  Similarly, <menu|Insert|Section> contains subsections and paragraphs, and
  in the <tmstyle|book> style <menu|Insert|Chapter|Chapter> starts a new chapter. A
  table of contents is generated by <menu|Insert|Automatic|Table of
  contents>, followed by <menu|Document|Update|All>.

